-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",208,{
[6625]="7001CC67\n1\tPatrol the road to the Gostannon\tThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angened, leading eastwards. The first patrol point lies to the north-west of Amon Angened, upon the road. Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.\n2\tPatrol the road to the Gostannon\tThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards. Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.\n3\tPatrol the road to the Gostannon\tThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards. Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.\n4\tPatrol the road to the Gostannon\tThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards. Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.\n5\tPatrol the road to the Gostannon\tThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards. Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.\n6\tTalk to Dannaswen atop Amon Angened\tDannaswen is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon. You should report back to Dannaswen at once.\n",
[6626]="7004E841\n1\tFind Dôm Goru\tDôm Goru can be found somewhere to the north-west of Furuk-mekhem, the Southgate. After learning that the Zhélruka have a small encampment named Dôm Goru in the eastern hills of the Ered Mithrin, Dori has asked you to ride ahead of the Company and learn if they know anything of Nori's expedition.\n2\tLearn if the Zhélruka at Dôm Goru encountered Nori's expedition\tDôm Goru can be found to the north-west of Furuk-mekhem, the Southgate in the Ered Mithrin. You have arrived at Dôm Goru and should now speak to the Zhélruka at the encampment and learn if they encountered Nori's expedition.\n3\tDefeat drakes and worms in the Grey Mountains (total: 14)\tDrakes and worms can be found throughout the Ered Mithrin. In exchange for information, Zádokh Flint-eye has asked you to defeat many of the drakes and worms of the Ered Mithrin.\n4\tTalk to Zádokh Flint-eye at Dôm Goru\tZádokh Flint-eye can be found at Dôm Goru in the Ered Mithrin. You have defeated many drakes and worms as Zádokh Flint-eye asked and should now return to him.\n5\tObtain a bag of gold coins\tBags of gold coins can be purchased at a Vault-keeper. In exchange for information, Zádokh Flint-eye has asked you to give him ten gold coins.\n6\tDeliver the bag of gold coins to Zádokh Flint-eye at Dôm Goru\tZádokh Flint-eye can be found at Dôm Goru in the Ered Mithrin. You have collected ten gold coins for Zádokh Flint-eye as he asked and should now speak to him.\n7\tFind a deposit of dragon-stone in the Bitter Scar\tDragon-stone could once be found in the depths of the Ered Mithrin and near to the lairs of dragons, but it might also be found among the Bitter Scar. Zádokh Flint-eye has asked you to find a deposit of dragon-stone in the Bitter Scar and bring a fragment of it to him.\n8\tCollect a fragment of dragon-stone\tA small deposit of dragon-stone can be found in the southernmost reaches of the Bitter Scar. You have discovered a deposit of dragon-stone and should now mine it for Zádokh Flint-eye.\n9\tDeliver the fragment of dragon-stone to Zádokh Flint-eye at Dôm Goru\tZádokh Flint-eye can be found at Dôm Goru. You have collected a small fragment of dragon-stone as Zádokh Flint-eye asked, and you should now deliver it to him at Dôm Goru and learn what else he knows of recent happenings in the Grey Mountains.\n10\tTalk to Dori at Dôm Goru\tDori can be found at Dôm Goru. After returning to Zádokh Flint-eye with the dragon-stone you discovered, he informed you that Dori and Company have come to Dôm Goru. You should speak to Dori and tell him what you have learned.\n",
[6627]="7005C8AB\n1\tFind Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate\tMúta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. After being discovered by Dourhands at the Witch-gate, Múta was captured and the rest of her scouts were scattered. You should find Múta.\n2\tTalk to Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate\tMúta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. Múta has been captured and imprisoned by the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. You should talk to Múta.\n3\tCollect orders from the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate (total: 3)\tDourhands can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. In preparation for her escape, Múta has asked you to collect orders from the Dourhands at the Witch-gate. You should defeat the Dourhands and collect their orders.\n4\tDeliver the orders to Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate\tMúta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. You have collected orders from the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. You should deliver them to Múta.\n5\tMúta's weapons can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. Múta has asked you to return her weapons to her before attempting an escape. You should collect Múta's weapons.\t\n6\tDeliver the weapons to Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate\tMúta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. You have recovered Múta's weapons. You should deliver them to Múta.\n",
[6628]="70061F04\n1\tBurn incense at barrows (total: 8)\tNan Mabli has asked you to burn incense at barrows in the South Downs. The barrows are located at Gond Orchal, in the South Downs.\n2\tReturn to Nan Mabli\tYou should let Nan Mabli know that you have burned incense at the barrows. Nan Mabli is at in the South Downs.\n",
[6629]="700529D0\n1\tFind the Orc camp of Brafulug\tLúfred has asked you to stop the Orc activity in Duskenvale so trade can resume. You should find the Orc camp in the hills in Duskenvale.\n2\tDefeat Orcs in Brafulug (total: 10)\030Defeat Captain Ugúrz\tYou have discovered a camp of Orcs in northern Duskenvale. You should defeat the Orcs and their leader in Brafulug.\n3\tTalk to Lúfred\tYou have defeated the Orcs in the hills of Duskenvale. You should return to Lúfred at the Beorning Watchpost to inform him.\n",
[6630]="700330C9\n1\tFind the heat source helping the grodbog hive\tYou seek the heat source helping the grodbog hive to incubate their young so quickly. It is likely found on the far side of the grodbog hive.\n2\tCheck out the noise around the corner to the right\tYou heard a noise when entering the Flaming Deeps from the Redhorn Lodes, coming from around the corner to the right.\n3\tCheck out the noise around the corner to the right\tYou found the heat source helping the grodbog hive, and sadly there is nothing that can be done to stop it. The hive has been built in the perfect location in Moria, to benefit from the natural heat production of the mines.\n",
[6631]="7000C37C\n1\tShow the orders to Elrond at Rivendell\tElrond is at the Last Homely House in Rivendell, south-west of Glóin's camp. Glóin realized that another set of orders written in the Black Speech would take too long to translate and sent you to Rivendell in order to speak with Elrond directly.\n2\tDeliver the orders to Glóin at his camp in the Misty Mountains\tGlóin is at his camp just outside of Goblin-town, north-east of Rivendell. Elrond Halfelven made marks upon the orders and warned you that the goblins had a new leader, a Great Goblin who was defiant of the Uruks' intrusion in Goblin-town. He sent you back to Glóin with the translated orders.\n",
[6632]="70042EDE\n1\tDefeat Haradrim Raiders near the farms (total: 9)\030Hide the seed stores (total: 6)\tLossarnach's seed stores can be found in the farms north-east of Arnach. You should travel to the remaining farms to the north-east and do what you can to hide and protect the seed stores there.\n2\tTalk to Indir\tIndir can be found in Arnach, near the keep. You should return to Indir and tell him that the remaining seed stores have been safely hidden from the foe.\n",
[6633]="70043290\n1\tWar-horns sabotaged (total: 4)\tWar-horns can be found in the Haradrim camps south and east of Arnach. Indir's men have seen great warhorns in the Haradrim camps. He believes that if you sabotaged the horns, any assault on Arnach would be disorganized.\n2\tTalk to Indir\tIndir can be found in Arnach, near the keep. Indir believes that if you sabotaged the Haradrim's war-horns, any assault on Arnach would be disorganized. You should return to him and tell him this has been done.\n",
[6634]="70042EDA\n1\tTear down Haradrim message ribbons (total: 8)\tThe message ribbons can be found east and south of Arnach. Haradrim scouts seem to be tying ribbons to trees to send each other messages. You should tear down as many of these ribbons as you can.\n2\tTalk to Indir\tIndir can be found in Arnach, near the keep. Haradrim scouts were tying ribbons to trees as a means of communicating. You have torn many of them down and should return to Indir to tell him.\n",
[6635]="70017528\n1\tBring the samples to Glorelloth at the Shadowed Refuge\030Collect spiny flesh (total: 12)\tSkûmfil lies to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Glorelloth wants to ensure that the kergrim are not responsible for the disease affecting the Orcs of the shadowy dark and so has sent you to collect samples of the kergrims' skin.\n",
[6636]="70048C9B\n1\tDefeat infected Orcs (total: 5)\tInfected Orcs can be found throughout Agarnaith. You should defeat infected Orcs.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[6637]="70017532\n1\tReturn the samples to Pentlenn at the Shadowed Refuge\030Collect strips of infected flesh (total: 18)\tThe Sixteenth Hall can be found north-east of the Shadowed Refuge. You should collect samples from defeated Orcs in the Sixteenth Hall to allow Pentlenn to observe the behaviour of this disease. He advised that you do your best to avoid becoming infected yourself.\n",
[6638]="70048C95\n1\tDefeat infected troll\tInfected trolls can be found in the wilds of Agarnaith. You should defeat infected trolls.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[6639]="700169CD\n1\tDefeat gredbyg (total: 12)\tThe gredbyg can be found to the south-west of the Orc-watch. Kúli has asked you to defeat the gredbyg which are driving him mad with their chittering.\n2\tTalk to Kúli\tKúli is alone at a camp far to the south-east of the Orc-watch, in a cavernous corridor between the Redhorn Lodes and the Flaming Deeps. Kúli will be pleased to know the chittering gredbyg have been silenced.\n",
[6640]="70032C35\n1\tDefeat grodbog warriors (total: 9)\tThe grodbog warriors can be found throughout the grodbog hive which takes up the entire cavernous corridor between the Redhorn Lodes and the Flaming Deeps. The droning noise from thousands of gredbyg is heard throughout most of Moria, but it's so constant most are unaware of it.\n2\tCompleted\tThe imposing grodbog hive takes up the entire cavernous corridor between the Redhorn Lodes and the Flaming Deeps. The droning is still painfully loud throughout the hive, but will be noticeably quieter in other parts of Moria.\n",
[6641]="7001D0CB\n1\tCollect fire-pots (total: 6)\030Burn oil-stores (total: 4)\tFire-pots and supply crates can be found in the Orc-forts throughout northern Gathbúrz. Thyrnir has asked you to destroy the goblins' stockpiles of fire-oil by igniting them with the goblins' own fire-pots.\n2\tTalk to Thyrnir at Thangúlhad\tThyrnir at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz. You should report your success to Thyrnir.\n",
[6642]="7001674E\n1\tDefeat Globsnaga Orcs (total: 8)\tGlobsnaga Orcs can be found at Dalgum-ru, south of the Shadowed Refuge. Tyki wants you to slay the Globsnaga Orcs in the area.\n2\tSpeak to Tyki at the Shadowed Refuge\tTyki is at the Shadowed Refuge, north of Dalgum-ru. You should return to Tyki and report that Dalgum-ru is indeed heavily infested with Orcs, and you have slain many.\n",
[6643]="70071611\n1\tDestroy grodbog hives (total: 10)\030Defeat gredbyg in Gnasher's Delf (total: 12)\tThe gredbyg have infested an area to the north of the Dawn-warden called Gnasher's Delf. You should defeat gredbyg and destroy the grodbog hives with the provided explosives at Gnasher's Delf.\n2\tTalk to Ashâb\tYou have reduced the grodbog numbers at Gnasher's Delf. You should return to Ashâb at the Dawn-warden.\n",
[6644]="7004E4C0\n1\tSpeak with Tuhâl and enter Instance: The Lord of Iron\tTuhâl is waiting to speak to Lord Náin on behalf of his people. Speak with Tuhâl to enter the instance 'Lord of Iron'.\n2\tTalk to Tuhâl\tTuhâl has convinced Lord Náin to give him time to evacuate the innocent Easterlings from Utterby. You should talk to Tuhâl.\n3\tTalk to Tuhâl\tTuhâl has fashioned you a disguise! You should talk to Tuhâl.\n4\tTravel to Utterby\tNow that you have a disguise, you need to infiltrate Er Shamol. You should travel to Utterby with Tuhâl.\n5\tTalk to Tuhâl\tTuhâl is ready to infiltrate Er Shamol. You should talk to Tuhâl.\n6\tTalk to Kunchat\tKunchat, who oversees the Jangovar's operations, will put you to work. You should talk to Kunchat.\n7\tUndermine the Jangovar by completing quests in Utterby\tUtterby is currently occupied by Jangovar forces. You should complete quests in Utterby to undermine the Jangovar.\n8\tFind and free Tuhâl's family\tTuhâl's family is somewhere in Utterby. You should find and free Tuhâl's family.\n9\tTalk to Kunchat\tKunchat, who oversees the Jangovar's forces, would like to speak with you. You should talk to Kunchat.\n",
[6645]="7004AB92\n1\tCompete in the pit-fighting tournament\tPárgrub can be found near Thorzhaf. You should talk to Párgrub and compete in the pit-fighting tournament.\n",
[6646]="70001858\n1\tTalk to Dagoras\tEsteldín is north-east of Lin Giliath, hidden within the eastern mountains between the Kingsfell and Nan Amlug. Aglardir has sent you to Dagoras, the watch-captain of Esteldín, to tell him of the passing of the Nazgûl.\n",
[6647]="7001A9A9\n1\tTalk to Chief Watcher Grimbriar\tChief Watcher Grimbriar is at his post outside Bree-town. Watchers Brittleleaf and Oakdale do not feel that the tide about crash over the walls of Andrath can be held back. They have asked you to convince Chief Watcher Grimbriar that he must seek the aid of the Rangers of the North.\n",
[6648]="7006A9EB\n1\tDeliver the letter to Porókho\tDeliver Belondor's letter to the Morutágya clan, informing them of the demise of their leader, Tumúldo Fierce-water.\n",
[6649]="700529E0\n1\tPlace goblin drawings (total: 15)\tIdeal drawing locations can be found inside Goblin-town. You should place goblin drawings in ideal drawing locations.\n2\tCompleted\tYou left some of the crude drawings at ideal locations within Goblin-town.\n",
[6650]="7006A9D7\n1\tCollect rye breads ([see journal]/5)\tKeteph wants you to collect five loaves of rye bread for him. He intends to try to infuse his latest recipe with a different bread from the north. Rye bread requires a cook proficient in Ironfold cooking. Seek out a cook with this skill or trade for the bread at the auction house.\n2\tDeliver the rye nread to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall\030Collect rye breads ([see journal]/5)\tYou have five loaves of rye to deliver to Keteph in the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[6651]="7006A9D4\n1\tDeliver Keteph's new recipe to Taphis\030Collect Keteph's Test Dish\030Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Hûzo\030Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Tankho\030Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Karishah in Rakhatâb\030Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Beliash in Rakhatâb\tKeteph wants discerning and brutally honest feedback from the workers of Rakhatâb. He asks that you deliver these free meals to the worker leaders there.\n2\tTalk to Keteph\tYou gathered the responses and critiques from the worker leaders in Rakhatâb. Return this information to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[6652]="7006A9D5\n1\tDeliver Keteph's latest recipe to Zerkho at the Expedition Camp\030Collect Keteph's Next Test Dish\030Deliver Keteph's latest recipe to Dorshet at the Expedition Camp\030Deliver Keteph's newest recipe to Karbah at the Expedition Camp\030Deliver Keteph's new recipe to Mallax at the Expedition Camp\030Deliver Keteph's latest recipe to Delona at the Expedition Camp\tKeteph asked that you take his deliveries to the scholars and artisans keeping busy at the expedition camp to the south-east of Umbar Baharbêl. Most are employees of the aristocrats who will be the final arbiters of his latest creation.\n2\tTalk to Keteph\tYou received nothing but goodwill and words of encouragement from the denizens of the expedition camp. It appears that Keteph's recipe is complete. Return to him at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[6653]="7006A9DF\n1\tCollect cabbages ([see journal]/5)\030Collect fresh carrots ([see journal]/5)\tKeteph asked you to find cabbages and carrots for his new dish. Apprentice farmers can grow carrots, and journeyman farmers can grow cabbages. Trade with a farmer or visit the auction house. Or, if you are lucky and patient, search the land for wild cabbages and carrots.\n2\tReturn the vegetables to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall\030Collect cabbages ([see journal]/5)\030Collect fresh carrots ([see journal]/5)\tReturn the fresh carrots and cabbages to Keteph at Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[6654]="7006A9D8\n1\tDeliver Keteph's Crab on Rye to Belondor at Dâr Laja\030Collect Keteph's Crab on Rye\030Deliver Keteph's Crab on Rye to Hármelak at Dâr Laja\030Deliver Keteph's Crab on Rye to Khôltekh at Dâr Laja\030Deliver Keteph's Crab on Rye to Rothog at Dâr Laja\tKeteph's latest recipe is complete. He asks for your assistance one last time to deliver his creation to the Kindred at Dâr Laja. Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall, is north of Swain's Guild-hall near the central crossroads of Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tTalk to Keteph\tThe Kindred all seemed to enjoy the dish. You should return to Keteph and inform him of his success.\n",
[6655]="7006A9DE\n1\tCollect five loaves of Barley Bread ([see journal]/5)\tAcquire five loaves of barley bread from cooks through trade or auction and return them to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl. Apprentice cooks can bake Barley Bread.\n2\tReturn the loaves of Barley Bread to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall\030Collect five loaves of Barley Bread ([see journal]/5)\tAcquire five loaves of barley bread from cooks through trade or auction and return them to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl. Apprentice cooks can bake barley bread.\n",
[6656]="7006A9DD\n1\tCollect Keteph's family cruet from Phâredar in Jax Phanâl\tReturn to Jax Phânal and speak with Phâredar to retrieve Keteph's family cruet.\n2\tCollect Keteph's family cruet\tPhâredar told you that Keteph's family cruet was stolen in a raid by goblins. She suggested that you go to the encampment in the south-east to acquire the cruet from the goblins.\n3\tDeliver the cruet to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall\tYou recovered Keteph's family cruet from the goblins. Return the cruet to him at Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
})
